    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2HhRMRf9gehPMXBKMQW3u1L)_\n\nBased on `main`, which already contains #193 (merged while this was written). #194 touches other files.\n\n## What\n- Query table specs get `:fold-tag` and `:fold-prop` (default `bib-parent`) and a new `:sections` column. Notes with the tag leave the table and are counted on the note their `bib-parent` link points at; that book is added if it is not a result itself.\n- The `Works` spec of `sp-author-notes` uses it: `:fold-tag \"booksection\"`, column `:sections` after `:title`.\n- Title decoration: the exc and vui renderers show the emoji of the note's tags (`sp-org-tag-groups`) in the title. The Org dblock title is an `id:` link, which `sp-org-tag-groups` already decorates in Org buffers, so no extra column or text is needed.\n\n## How booksections link to the book\nThrough the meta key `bib-parent` (`- bib-parent :: [[id:...]]`), required by the `booksection` schema, target tag `book`.\n\n## Not changed\n`Works` blocks that already exist keep their old spec. Add `:fold-tag \"booksection\" :fold-prop \"bib-parent\"` and the `:sections` column by hand.\n\n## Tested\n2 new ERT tests (fold, no-op) in Emacs 29.3 batch with stubbed notes; the 11 `sp-author-notes` tests pass. Six older dblock tests in `sp-collection-query-tables-test.el` fail in my container with or without this change. Not tested: real vault, Vulpea database, emoji in the Org block, exc/vui on screen.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9EUSzAa9FcegNhKcw)_",
